<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <a href="/docs/scripting" class="inline-flex items-center text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300 font-medium transition-colors group">
      <svg class="w-4 h-4 mr-2 transform group-hover:-translate-x-1 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path></svg>
      Lua Scripting Overview
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-12">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="relative">
      <div class="absolute -inset-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-indigo-600 rounded-lg blur opacity-25"></div>
      <div class="relative">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-400 via-indigo-400 to-purple-400 mb-4 tracking-tight">Database Access</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-300 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
          Interact with data, execute queries, and run transactions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CRUD Operations -->
    <section id="crud">
      <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
        <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center mt-0 border-0">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-green-500 mr-2"></span>
            CRUD Operations
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="p-8">
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-4">The <code>db</code> global is bound to the database the script was invoked under (the <code>{db}</code> segment of the URL). It has four methods; all document operations go through a collection handle.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-3 font-mono text-sm text-gray-300">
            <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
              <span class="text-purple-400">db:collection(name)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; collection</span>
              <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Get a handle with <code>get / insert / update / delete / count / find / find_one / bulk_insert / upsert</code>. See <a href="#collection" class="text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300">Collection Object</a> below.</div>
            </li>
            <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
              <span class="text-purple-400">db:query(sdbql, bind_vars?)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; array</span>
              <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Run an SDBQL query and get the rows as a Lua array.</div>
            </li>
            <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
              <span class="text-purple-400">db:query_json(sdbql, bind_vars?)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; string</span>
              <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Same query, but the result is returned already serialised as JSON. Cheaper than <code>json.encode(db:query(...))</code> when the rows are only passed through to the client.</div>
            </li>
            <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
              <span class="text-purple-400">db:transaction(function(tx) ... end)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; success, result|error</span>
              <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Run the function inside an ACID transaction. See <a href="#transactions" class="text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300">Transactions</a>.</div>
            </li>
          </ul>

          <div class="mt-6 bg-yellow-500/10 border border-yellow-500/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <div class="flex items-start">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-yellow-400 mr-3 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>
              <div>
                <h4 class="text-yellow-400 font-semibold mb-1">Scripts act as their caller</h4>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">
                  There are no <code>db:get</code>/<code>db:insert</code> shortcuts, and no elevated "script user". Every read and write runs under the principal that invoked the endpoint:
                  <code>db:query</code> applies that user's row policies (admins are exempt), and writes are authorised the same way as the HTTP API.
                  Ordinary collections are unrestricted, <code>_jobs</code> needs an admin caller, and the collections the server executes or reads back for authorisation
                  (<code>_scripts</code>, <code>_services</code>, <code>_triggers</code>, <code>_views</code>, <code>_graphs</code>, <code>_config</code>, <code>_rag_pipelines</code>, and the credential collections)
                  are never writable from a script: the attempt fails with a 403.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SDBQL Queries -->
    <section id="queries">
      <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
        <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center mt-0 border-0">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-blue-500 mr-2"></span>
            SDBQL Queries
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="p-8">
           <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">
             Execute complex queries using SDBQL (SoliDB Query Language).
           </p>
           <div class="bg-gray-950 rounded-xl border border-white/10 overflow-hidden shadow-xl mb-6">
                <div class="p-4 font-mono text-sm text-gray-300">
<pre class="language-lua"><span class="text-blue-400">local</span> results = <span class="text-purple-400">db:query</span>(<span class="text-green-400">"FOR u IN users FILTER u.age > @age RETURN u"</span>, {
  age = <span class="text-purple-400">18</span>
})

<span class="text-blue-400">for</span> _, user <span class="text-blue-400">in</span> <span class="text-blue-400">ipairs</span>(results) <span class="text-blue-400">do</span>
  <span class="text-purple-400">solidb.log</span>(<span class="text-green-400">"User: "</span> .. user.name)
<span class="text-blue-400">end</span>

<span class="text-gray-500">-- Pass-through endpoint: skip the Lua round-trip and hand the JSON straight back</span>
<span class="text-blue-400">return</span> response.json(<span class="text-purple-400">db:query_json</span>(<span class="text-green-400">"FOR u IN users LIMIT 100 RETURN u"</span>))</pre>
                </div>
           </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Transactions -->
    <section id="transactions">
      <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
        <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center mt-0 border-0">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-yellow-500 mr-2"></span>
            ACID Transactions with Row-Level Locking
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="p-8">
           <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">
             Perform atomic operations across multiple collections using <code>db:transaction</code>. 
             Transactions use <strong>row-level locking</strong> - each document is independently locked.
           </p>
           <div class="bg-gray-950 rounded-xl border border-white/10 overflow-hidden shadow-xl mb-6">
               <div class="p-4 font-mono text-sm text-gray-300">
<pre class="language-lua"><span class="text-blue-400">local</span> success, err = <span class="text-purple-400">db:transaction</span>(<span class="text-blue-400">function</span>(tx)
  <span class="text-gray-500">-- Get collection handle within transaction</span>
  <span class="text-blue-400">local</span> accounts = tx:collection(<span class="text-green-300">"accounts"</span>)
  
  <span class="text-gray-500">-- Read operations acquire SHARED locks (multiple readers allowed)</span>
  <span class="text-blue-400">local</span> sender = accounts:get(<span class="text-green-300">"A"</span>)
  <span class="text-blue-400">local</span> receiver = accounts:get(<span class="text-green-300">"B"</span>)

  <span class="text-blue-400">if</span> sender.balance &lt; <span class="text-purple-400">100</span> <span class="text-blue-400">then</span>
    <span class="text-blue-400">error</span>(<span class="text-green-300">"Insufficient funds"</span>) <span class="text-gray-500">-- Will rollback automatically</span>
  <span class="text-blue-400">end</span>

  <span class="text-gray-500">-- Write operations acquire EXCLUSIVE locks</span>
  accounts:update(<span class="text-green-300">"A"</span>, { balance = sender.balance - <span class="text-purple-400">100</span> })
  accounts:update(<span class="text-green-300">"B"</span>, { balance = receiver.balance + <span class="text-purple-400">100</span> })

  <span class="text-blue-400">return</span> <span class="text-green-300">"Transfer complete"</span>
<span class="text-blue-400">end</span>)

<span class="text-blue-400">if</span> <span class="text-blue-400">not</span> success <span class="text-blue-400">then</span>
  <span class="text-purple-400">solidb.log</span>(<span class="text-green-300">"Tx failed: "</span> .. err)
<span class="text-blue-400">end</span></pre>
               </div>
           </div>

           <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Transaction API</h3>
           <ul class="space-y-3 font-mono text-sm text-gray-300 mb-6">
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-3 rounded border border-white/5">
               <span class="text-purple-400">db:transaction(fn)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; success, result | error</span>
               <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Runs <code>fn(tx)</code>. Commits when it returns and yields <code>true, value</code>; any error rolls everything back and yields <code>false, message</code>.</div>
             </li>
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-3 rounded border border-white/5">
               <span class="text-purple-400">tx:collection(name)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; table</span>
               <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Get a transactional collection handle. It exposes only <code>get</code>, <code>insert</code>, <code>update</code> and <code>delete</code>; run queries and bulk operations outside the transaction.</div>
             </li>
           </ul>

           <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Collection Methods within Transaction</h3>
           <ul class="space-y-3 font-mono text-sm text-gray-300 mb-6">
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-3 rounded border border-cyan-500/30">
               <span class="text-cyan-400">collection:get(key)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; table|nil</span>
               <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1"><strong>Shared lock</strong> - Read a document. Multiple transactions can read simultaneously.</div>
             </li>
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-3 rounded border border-amber-500/30">
               <span class="text-amber-400">collection:insert(doc)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; table</span>
               <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1"><strong>Exclusive lock</strong> - Insert new document. Returns the stored document, including its generated <code>_key</code>.</div>
             </li>
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-3 rounded border border-amber-500/30">
               <span class="text-amber-400">collection:update(key, doc)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; table</span>
               <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1"><strong>Exclusive lock</strong> - Update existing document.</div>
             </li>
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-3 rounded border border-amber-500/30">
               <span class="text-amber-400">collection:delete(key)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; bool</span>
               <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1"><strong>Exclusive lock</strong> - Delete document.</div>
             </li>
           </ul>

           <div class="mt-4 p-4 bg-cyan-500/10 border border-cyan-500/20 rounded-lg">
             <div class="flex items-start">
               <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-cyan-400 mr-3 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>
               <div>
                 <h4 class="text-cyan-400 font-semibold mb-1">Row-Level Locking</h4>
                 <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">
                   <strong>Shared locks</strong> (reads): Multiple transactions can read the same document.<br>
                   <strong>Exclusive locks</strong> (writes): Only one transaction can modify a document.<br>
                   Locks are acquired on first access and held until commit/rollback.
                 </p>
               </div>
             </div>
           </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <!-- Collection Object -->
    <section id="collection">
      <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
        <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center mt-0 border-0">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-indigo-500 mr-2"></span>
            Collection Object
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="p-8">
          <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">
            Access collections directly via <code>db:collection("name")</code> for cleaner, scoped operations.
          </p>
          <div class="bg-gray-950 rounded-xl border border-white/10 overflow-hidden shadow-xl mb-6">
            <div class="p-4 font-mono text-sm text-gray-300">
<pre class="language-lua"><span class="text-blue-400">local</span> users = <span class="text-purple-400">db:collection</span>(<span class="text-green-400">"users"</span>)

<span class="text-gray-500">-- CRUD operations</span>
<span class="text-blue-400">local</span> user = users:<span class="text-purple-400">get</span>(<span class="text-green-400">"alice"</span>)              <span class="text-gray-500">-- Get by _key</span>
<span class="text-blue-400">local</span> bob = users:<span class="text-purple-400">insert</span>({name = <span class="text-green-400">"Bob"</span>})       <span class="text-gray-500">-- Insert, returns the document (bob._key)</span>
<span class="text-blue-400">local</span> alice = users:<span class="text-purple-400">update</span>(<span class="text-green-400">"alice"</span>, {age = <span class="text-purple-400">30</span>}) <span class="text-gray-500">-- Merge, returns the updated document</span>
users:<span class="text-purple-400">delete</span>(<span class="text-green-400">"alice"</span>)                     <span class="text-gray-500">-- Delete document, returns true</span>

<span class="text-gray-500">-- Querying (operator keys need the ["$op"] form in Lua)</span>
<span class="text-blue-400">local</span> adults = users:<span class="text-purple-400">find</span>({ age = { [<span class="text-green-400">"$gte"</span>] = <span class="text-purple-400">18</span> } })   <span class="text-gray-500">-- Find with filter</span>
<span class="text-blue-400">local</span> bob = users:<span class="text-purple-400">find_one</span>({name = <span class="text-green-400">"Bob"</span>})       <span class="text-gray-500">-- Find single document</span>
<span class="text-blue-400">local</span> count = users:<span class="text-purple-400">count</span>()                   <span class="text-gray-500">-- Count all documents</span>

<span class="text-gray-500">-- Bulk operations</span>
users:<span class="text-purple-400">bulk_insert</span>({                         <span class="text-gray-500">-- Insert multiple</span>
  {name = <span class="text-green-400">"User1"</span>},
  {name = <span class="text-green-400">"User2"</span>},
  {name = <span class="text-green-400">"User3"</span>}
})

users:<span class="text-purple-400">upsert</span>(<span class="text-green-400">"user-key"</span>, {name = <span class="text-green-400">"Updated"</span>})  <span class="text-gray-500">-- Insert or update</span></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Collection Methods</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-3 font-mono text-sm text-gray-300">
            <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
              <span class="text-purple-400">collection:get(key)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; table|nil</span>
              <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Get document by <strong>_key</strong> (not _id). Returns nil if not found.</div>
            </li>
            <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
              <span class="text-purple-400">collection:insert(doc)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; table</span>
              <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Insert document. Uses <code>_key</code> if provided, or generates UUID v7. Returns the full stored document (<code>_key</code>, <code>_id</code>, <code>_rev</code> and fields).</div>
            </li>
            <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
              <span class="text-purple-400">collection:update(key, doc)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; table</span>
              <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Update document by key. Merges fields with existing document and returns the full updated document.</div>
            </li>
            <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
              <span class="text-purple-400">collection:delete(key)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; bool</span>
              <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Delete document by key. Returns true on success.</div>
            </li>
            <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
              <span class="text-purple-400">collection:count()</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; number</span>
              <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Count all documents in the collection. For a conditional count use <code>db:query</code> with <code>COLLECT WITH COUNT</code>.</div>
            </li>
            <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
              <span class="text-purple-400">collection:find(filter)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; table[]</span>
              <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Find all documents matching filter criteria. Equality is <code>{ name = "Bob" }</code>; operators use bracketed keys: <code>{ age = { ["$gte"] = 18 } }</code>. An empty table returns everything.</div>
            </li>
            <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
              <span class="text-purple-400">collection:find_one(filter)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; table|nil</span>
              <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Find first document matching filter. Returns nil if not found.</div>
            </li>
            <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
              <span class="text-purple-400">collection:bulk_insert(docs)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; table[]</span>
              <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Insert array of documents efficiently. Returns array of inserted documents.</div>
            </li>
            <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
              <span class="text-purple-400">collection:upsert(key_or_filter, doc)</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-&gt; table</span>
              <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Insert if not exists, update if exists. Accepts key string or filter table.</div>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <div class="mt-6 bg-yellow-500/10 border border-yellow-500/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <div class="flex items-start">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-yellow-400 mr-3 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>
              <div>
                <h4 class="text-yellow-400 font-semibold mb-1">Important: get() uses _key, not _id</h4>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">
                  The <code>collection:get()</code> method expects just the document key, not the full _id format (<code>collection/key</code>).
                  <br><br>
                  <strong>Correct:</strong> <code>users:get("019c243e-9d0b-756c-be78-e4cad62fa2a1")</code><br>
                  <strong>Wrong:</strong> <code>users:get("users/019c243e-9d0b-756c-be78-e4cad62fa2a1")</code>
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
